// check: accepted
// CROWN — the latent half at the DEFAULT PARAMETER carrier: a default
// whose value is an effectful closure TRANSPORTS under `with !E` as long
// as nothing calls it. The effect rides the value; only performing it is
// a performance, and the gate must not over-reject the carrier itself.
//
// The pair is each other's evidence: add `b()` to this body and it
// becomes leak-default-latent, which rejects. Both were measured before
// either landed, because the wheel writes no default-valued parameter at
// all and no other gate here can go red.
effect E { op() -> Int }

fn takes(a, b = () => op()) = a

fn good() with !E = takes(1)

fn main() = good()
